From: gts9wifi Ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: mask the ready IRQ after the first signal

With the handover IRQ masked (Ultra's q6v5 patch, 0009) the SM8550 ADSP
on the X710 still pulses its SMP2P "ready" edge: 342 interrupts in the
first ~67 s after the ADSP came up, ~5/s for the whole uptime, each one
waking a CPU for a completion that was already done.

Mask it after the first signal and unmask it in qcom_q6v5_prepare(), so
every remoteproc start still sees exactly one ready completion.  Not yet
built or tested on the tablet: goes in with the next kernel build.

---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.h	2026-10-19 01:01:24.262092669 +0300
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.h	2026-10-19 01:01:24.278103293 +0300
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 	int stop_irq;
 
 	bool handover_issued;
+	bool ready_masked;
 
 	struct completion start_done;
 	struct completion stop_done;
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c	2026-10-19 01:01:24.260063820 +0300
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c	2026-10-19 01:01:24.278186848 +0300
@@ -65,6 +65,10 @@
 	q6v5->handover_issued = false;
 
 	enable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
+	if (q6v5->ready_masked) {
+		q6v5->ready_masked = false;
+		enable_irq(q6v5->ready_irq);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -140,6 +144,17 @@
 
 	complete(&q6v5->start_done);
 
+	/*
+	 * Like handover, ready is one notification per start, but Samsung's
+	 * SM8550 ADSP keeps pulsing it (about five times a second on the
+	 * SM-X710), waking a CPU each time.  Mask it once the start is
+	 * signalled; prepare() unmasks it for the next start.
+	 */
+	if (!q6v5->ready_masked) {
+		q6v5->ready_masked = true;
+		disable_irq_nosync(irq);
+	}
+
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
